{"id": "86110", "name": "פירוק מספר לגורמים ראשוניים – כתיבה כמכפלת חזקות (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Factorise \\({{CT:0}}\\) into primes:</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div><p style=\"font-size:0.92em;margin:8px 0 0\">Write your answer as powers of primes, e.g. \\(p_1^{n_1}\\times\\cdots\\).</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Divide repeatedly by the smallest prime that divides the number, until the quotient is \\(1\\); then collect equal primes into powers.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Repeated division by primes</b><br>To factorise a number into primes the best trick is to divide by the smallest prime, \\(2\\), as long as the result is an integer. When \\(2\\) no longer divides, try the next prime, \\(3\\), then \\(5\\), \\(7\\), and so on, until the quotient is \\(1\\). In the table, each row shows the current number (left) and the prime it is divided by (right); the next row holds the quotient:<table dir=\"ltr\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px auto\"><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 12px;text-align:right\">\\({{